# Rust
/target/
**/target/
**/*.rs.bk

# WebAssembly build output (wasm-pack / wasm-bindgen / trunk)
/pkg/
**/pkg/
*.wasm

# Generated TypeScript for the wasm boundary's wire types (ts-rs, via `pnpm run build:bindings`).
# Stands to `web/src` as `/pkg/` above does — generated from the Rust declarations rather than
# written, so there is no committed copy that can go stale. Deliberately NOT
# under `web/src/`, which would put generated files inside biome's `files.includes` and have it
# reformat and lint them.
/web/bindings/

# ...and the scratch directories `scripts/build-web-bindings.sh` uses to swap a fresh generation into
# `/web/bindings/` above without ever deleting the last-good copy before the new one is ready. Named
# per-process (`mktemp`'s random suffix, `.old` appended for the swap's holding spot) so two concurrent
# runs can never collide on either name — see that script's header for why a fixed shared name was a
# Critical this glob replaces. Present only mid-regeneration, or if a run was killed before cleaning up
# after itself; `/web/bindings.lock/` is the mutex directory the swap itself is guarded by, present only
# while a run holds it or if a run was killed while holding it.
/web/bindings.tmp.*/
/web/bindings.lock/

# ...and the crate-relative copy `cargo test -p redextape-core --features ts` (or
# `-p redextape-wasm`) writes when TS_RS_EXPORT_DIR is unset. `scripts/check-all.sh` exports it so the
# gate never lands here, but a developer running that cargo command directly still does — ts-rs
# resolves the variable against each crate's manifest directory, so "unset" means "beside the crate",
# not "nowhere".
crates/*/bindings/

# Web frontend
node_modules/
dist/
.vite/
coverage/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Vitest browser-mode artifacts. Written only when a browser test FAILS, so they are absent on a
# green tree and would otherwise be committed by whoever happens to run the suite after a red one.
.vitest-attachments/
**/__screenshots__/

# Environment & secrets
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Logs, editor, OS cruft
*.log
.DS_Store
.idea/

# Agent worktrees
/.claude/worktrees/

# Repo-local dev tooling scripts/setup-dev.sh installs (e.g. the pinned tree-sitter CLI), so a
# developer's machine matches what CI runs without polluting $PATH or a system directory.
/.tools/

# Playwright MCP session output — screenshots and page snapshots from browser-driving tools.
# Never source; regenerated on demand and easily swept in by `git add -A`.
.playwright-mcp/
# ...and stray screenshots a browser tool wrote to a relative path outside it.
redextape-*.png

# `tree-sitter build -o parser.so` writes here, and it is an EDITOR that runs it rather than anything
# in this repository: nvim-treesitter's local-path install compiles in place, inside whichever
# checkout it was pointed at. `plugin/redextape.lua` points it at this one, so a developer who
# installs the grammars through Neovim gets four untracked binaries in a tree that was clean before.
# Not swept up by `/target/` above — these sit beside the committed `src/parser.c`, not under it.
grammars/*/parser.so
